{"id": "yph2_v1_u5_c1_pdf016_0072", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 5, "unit_name": "Further Mechanics", "chapter_no": 1, "chapter_title": "5A Further Momentum", "section": "IMPULSE", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [6, 6], "pdf_pages": [16, 16], "char_count": 375, "text": "IMPULSE\n\nTheproductofa force appliedforaknowntime(Fxt)isknown as theimpulse,and thisisequal tothechangeinmomentum:\n\nimpulse(Ns)=force(N)xtime(s)\n\n=change in momentum (kgms-1)\n\nimpulse\n\n=F×t=p\n\nTostopsomethingmovingweneedtoremoveallofits momentum.Thisideaallowsustocalculatetheimpulseneeded tostopanobjectmoving.Ifweknowhowlongaforceisapplied wecouldworkoutthesizeofthatforce."}
