{"id": "yph2_v1_u6_c3_pdf036_0148", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 6, "unit_name": "Electric and Magnetic Fields", "chapter_no": 3, "chapter_title": "6A Electric Fields", "section": "CHAPTER 6A ELECTRICFIELDS", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [26, 26], "pdf_pages": [36, 36], "char_count": 1029, "text": "CHAPTER 6A ELECTRICFIELDS\n\nThe usual explanationfor thespikyhaircaused by touchingaVande Graaffgeneratoristhatthe excesscharges it puts on the body all repel each other,so eachhair experiences a forcepushing it away from the others and from thehead.Whilstthisistrue,the explanationistoosimple.Thehairshowsusthe existence of an electric field comingfrom the person's head,with the hair trying to follow the electricfield lines. Gravity also affects the hair,so thereisaresultantforce effect.lfyour school has aVan deGraaffgenerator,youcould trysettingup an experiment where the person in contactwith it is in different positions(i.e. lying down on a wooden bench, bending overat thewaist,etc.),so that the electrical andgravitational forces arenotworking againsteach other quitesomuch!\n\nIn thischapter,wewillseethedifferencebetweenuniformandradial fields,andlearnhowtocalculatethe strengthofbothtypesof electricfield.Wewill also explore theconceptof electricpotential,whichrelates to the storage and delivery of electrical energy."}
