{"id": "yph2_v1_u6_c4_pdf059_0241", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 6, "unit_name": "Electric and Magnetic Fields", "chapter_no": 4, "chapter_title": "6B Capacitors", "section": "DISCHARGINGCAPACITORMATHS CHARGE,Q", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [49, 49], "pdf_pages": [59, 59], "char_count": 652, "text": "DISCHARGINGCAPACITORMATHS CHARGE,Q\n\nWe have seen that thecharging and dischargingofa capacitor follows curvinggraphsinwhich the current is constantly changing.It follows that therate ofchange ofchargeandp.d.are also constantly changing.Thesegraphs areknown asexponential curves.The shapes canbeproduced byplottingmathematicalformulaewhichhavepowerfunctionsinthem.Inthecaseofdischarginga capacitor,C,througharesistor,R,thefunctionthatdescribesthechargeremainingonthecapacitor Q,at a time,,is:\n\nQ=Qoe-/RC\n\nwhereQistheinitial charge onthecapacitoratt=O,andeisthespecialmathematicalnumber which is used in theinverse function of natural logarithms(e2.718)."}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u6_c4_pdf059_0242", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 6, "unit_name": "Electric and Magnetic Fields", "chapter_no": 4, "chapter_title": "6B Capacitors", "section": "WORKEDEXAMPLE1", "content_type": "worked_example", "book_pages": [49, 49], "pdf_pages": [59, 59], "char_count": 276, "text": "WORKEDEXAMPLE1\n\nA 0.03Fcapacitorisfullycharged by a12V supply and is then connected to discharge througha900Q resistor.Howmuchchargeremainson thecapacitorafter20 seconds?\n\nInitialcharge,Qo=CV=0.03x12=0.36C\n\nQ=Qoe-/RC\n\nQ=0.36×e(-20/(900×0.03)=0.36xe(-20/27)=0.36x0.477\n\nQ=0.17C"}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u6_c4_pdf059_0243", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 6, "unit_name": "Electric and Magnetic Fields", "chapter_no": 4, "chapter_title": "6B Capacitors", "section": "VOLTAGE,V", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [49, 49], "pdf_pages": [59, 59], "char_count": 280, "text": "VOLTAGE,V\n\nQ=CVintoourexponential decayequation,wecanshowtheformulathatdescribesvoltageona dischargingcapacitorisinexactlythe sameform asforthechargeitself\n\n（which also means that initially,Q。=CV)\n\nCV=CVoe-t/RC\n\nfromwhich the capacitance term,C,canbecancelled,leaving:\n\nV=Voe-t/RC"}
