{"id": "yph2_v1_u7_c6_pdf086_0346", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 7, "unit_name": "Nuclear and Particle Physics", "chapter_no": 6, "chapter_title": "7A Probing Matter", "section": "CHADWICK'SDISCOVERYOFTHENEUTRON", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [76, 76], "pdf_pages": [86, 86], "char_count": 1359, "text": "CHADWICK'SDISCOVERYOFTHENEUTRON\n\nRutherforddetermined thatmostof the atom'smassand all thepositivechargewasheldinavery smallnucleusinthecentre,and thatelectronswereattheedgeoftheatom.Thedifferencebetween thenuclearmassandthekmownnumberofprotonsinitcausedaproblemthough.Nucleiweretoo massiveconsideringthenumberofprotonstheycontained.Rutherfordsuggestedthatadditional proton-electronpairs,bound together,were theextramassinthenucleus.\n\nIn1930,IreneJoliot-CurieandherhusbandFredericfoundthatalphaparticleshittingberyllium wouldcauseittogiveoffanunkmownradiation.Difficulttodetect,thisunknown,uncharged radiationcouldremoveprotonsfromparaffinandtheseweredetectedbyaGeiger-Mullertube.\n\nTheJoliot-Curiestriedtoexplaintheunknownradiationasgammarays,butastheserayshaveno mass,thiswasagainsttherulesoftheconservationofmomentum.JamesChadwickrepeatedthe experiments(figD)alsousingothertargetmaterials.Chadwickconsideredmomentumtransferand conservationofkineticenergyinthecollisionsbetweentheparticlesandheconcludedthatthe berylliumradiationwasaneutralparticlewhichhadamassabout1%morethanthatofaproton.In 1932,hepublishedaproposalfortheexistenceofthisnewparticle,whichhecalledaneutron,andn 1935hewasawardedtheNobelprizeforthisdiscovery.\n\nfigDChadwick'sexperimenttodeterminetheexistenceoftheneutronreliedon theconservationofmomentum to workoutthemassofthisneutralparticle"}
