{"id": "yph2_v1_u7_c6_pdf089_0361", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 7, "unit_name": "Nuclear and Particle Physics", "chapter_no": 6, "chapter_title": "7A Probing Matter", "section": "SKILLS", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [79, 79], "pdf_pages": [89, 89], "char_count": 842, "text": "SKILLS\n\nSELF-DIRECTIONADAPTIVEEARNINGINTERPRETATION COMMUNICATION,ADAPTABILITY\n\n• CalculatethedeBrogliewavelengthsforthefollowing:\n\n• (a)anelectrontravellingat2%of thespeedof light\n\n• (b)anelectronwhichhasbeenaccelerated through1200v\n\n• （c)aprotonwithamomentumof5x10-21kgms-1\n\n• (d)yourunningat5ms-).\n\n• 2. WhywoulddeBroglienothavebeenawardedtheNobelPrize beforetheDavisson-Germerexperiment?\n\n• 3. Calculatethespeedatwhichanelectronmusttravelifitistobe usedtoprobethestructureofthenucleus.(Itwouldneedade Brogliewavelengthofaboutthesizeof thenucleus: =5×10-15m.)Commentonyouranswer.\n\n• Carryoutsomeresearchtofindouthowthedirectionofthe electronbeaminacathoderayoscilloscope(CRO)canbe changedinordertomake anypointonthescreenlightup. Showthisinadiagram.ExplainhowsuchaCROcouldbeset upinahospitaltodisplaytheelectricalimpulsesofapatients heart."}
