{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf129_0528", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "Investigatingthermostats", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [119, 119], "pdf_pages": [129, 129], "char_count": 1089, "text": "Investigatingthermostats\n\nInBook1,Section4B.3,wesawhowapotentialdividercircuitcan beusedwithasensorcomponenttocontrolasecondcircuit.This canbeuseful,forexampleifwewanttocontrolaheatingorcooling circuit,suchaswiththecircuitshowninfig.\n\nfigCInvestigatehowthe motor(C) speed adjustsasthe thermistor(A) temperatureisaltered.Thiscircuitcouldbe used tocontrola coolingfan.\n\nManyelectroniccomponentshaveaswitchonvoltageof5V.For example,thecontrolcircuittoswitchonalargeairconditionercould beusedwithathermistorinapotentialdividercircuitandwould onlyswitchonwhenthep.d.acrossitis5V.Alteringthevalueofthe otherresistorinthepotentialdividercircuitwouldthencontrolthe temperaturelevelatwhichtheairconditionerwasswitchedon.\n\nYoucanuseacircuit likethatshowninfigCtofind theoutput voltageatdifferenttemperaturestocalibratethethermistor.This calibrationshouldthenallowyoutoreplacethefixedresistorwitha variableresistorthatyoucanset,sothattheoutputexceeds5volts onlywhenaparticulartemperatureisreached.\n\nSafetyNote:Becareful nottooverloadthecomponentsin the circuit as they may get hot enough toburn skin."}
