{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf129_0532", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "SUBJECT VOCABULARY", "content_type": "subject_vocabulary", "book_pages": [119, 119], "pdf_pages": [129, 129], "char_count": 536, "text": "SUBJECT VOCABULARY\n\nkinetictheorytheidea thatconsiderationof themicroscopic movementsofparticleswillpredictthemacroscopicbehaviour ofasubstance\n\nabsolutezerothetheoretical temperatureatwhichmoleculeswill no longerbe moving,all kineticenergy hasbeen removed\n\nCelsiusscale a scaleof temperaturewithzero degrees at the freezing pointofwater,and100degreesattheboilingpointofwater\n\nKelvinscale an absolute temperaturescalewith eachdegree the samesize asthoseontheCelsiusscale\n\nabsolutetemperature a temperaturescale thatstartsat absolutezero"}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf130_0533", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "LEARNING OBJECTIVES", "content_type": "learning_objectives", "book_pages": [120, 120], "pdf_pages": [130, 130], "char_count": 848, "text": "LEARNING OBJECTIVES\n\n• Define theconceptsofspecificheatcapacity andspecificlatentheatforphasechanges.\n\n• Use theequationsE=mc△θ andE=L△m\n\nWehaveseenthatthetemperatureofasubstancedependsonthekineticenergyofthemolecules withinit.Asthemoleculesmove,theirbondscanpullonneighbouringmolecules.Thismeansthat latticevibrationsinthesolidcanpassenergythroughthesolid.\n\nImaginethatoneendofa longrodisbeingheated.Inthehotterpartsofthemetal,themolecules arevibratingfasterandfurtherInthecoolerpartsoftherod,furtherfromtheheatsource,the moleculesaremovingslowerWhenamoleculewithmoreenergypullsononewithlessenergy,they sharetheenergymoreevenly,withthefasteroneslowingdownandthesloweronespeedingup.The effectofthesetransfersisthat theincreaseintheinternal kineticenergywhichiscausedbyheating movesthroughoutasubstance,withtheheatpassingfromhotterareastocolderones."}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf130_0534", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "SPECIFICHEATCAPACITY", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [120, 120], "pdf_pages": [130, 130], "char_count": 1012, "text": "SPECIFICHEATCAPACITY\n\nTransferring thesame amount ofheatenergyto two different objectswillincrease theirinternal energybythesame amount.However,thiswill notnecessarilycausethesameriseintemperature inboth.Howtransferred heatenergyaffectsthetemperatureofanobjectdependsonthreethings:\n\n• 1theamount ofheatenergytransferred\n\n• 2themassoftheobject\n\n• 3thespecificheatcapacityofthematerialfromwhichtheobjectismade\n\nHowmuchthetemperaturerisesdependsonthematerial,andisgivenbyapropertyknownasits specifcheatcapacity,c.Differentmaterialsanddifferentphasesofthesamesubstance,have differentspecificheatcapacitiesbecausetheirmolecularstructuresaredifferent.Thismeansthat theirmoleculeswillbeaffected todifferentdegreesby additional heatenergy.\n\nrelatedtothemassofmaterial,m,and thespecificheatcapacity,c,bytheexpression：\n\nWitheachquantitymeasuredinSIunits,thismeansthatthespecificheatcapacityhasunitsof Jkg-K-1.Thechangeintemperature.o,is thesamewhethermeasuredindegreescelsiusorkelvin, astheintervalsarethesameonbothscales."}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf130_0535", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "WORKEDEXAMPLE1", "content_type": "worked_example", "book_pages": [120, 120], "pdf_pages": [130, 130], "char_count": 336, "text": "WORKEDEXAMPLE1\n\nHowlongwilla2kWkettletake toraisethetemperatureof800gramsofwaterfrom20°Cto100°C?The specificheat capacity of water is4200jkg-K-1\n\n△0=100-20=80°C=80K\n\n△E=mc△0=0.8×4200×80=268800j\n\nThereforethekettletakes2minutesand14secondstoheatthiswatertoboilingtemperature.Weassume that no energy is wasted in heating the surroundings."}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf130_0536", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "LEARNING TIP", "content_type": "learning_tip", "book_pages": [120, 120], "pdf_pages": [130, 130], "char_count": 174, "text": "LEARNING TIP\n\nHeat isonlyreferred towhen energy ismovedfromone objectormaterial to another.lt isincorrectto suggestthat an objecthasheatenergy.Werefer to its'internal energy."}
