{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf135_0566", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "EXAM HINT", "content_type": "exam_hint", "book_pages": [125, 125], "pdf_pages": [135, 135], "char_count": 321, "text": "EXAM HINT\n\nSafetyNote:Weareyeprotection andmakesure all theconnections aresecure toavoid highpressure leaks.Reduce thepressurebefore disconnectingthepump.\n\nMakesureyou haveagood understandingof thispractical as yourunderstandingof the experimental methodmaybe assessed inyourexams.\n\nfigAApparatustodemonstrate Boyle'slaw."}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u8_c9_pdf136_0567", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 8, "unit_name": "Thermodynamics", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "8A Heat and Temperature", "section": "CHARLES'SLAW", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [126, 126], "pdf_pages": [136, 136], "char_count": 372, "text": "CHARLES'SLAW\n\nAbout140yearsafterBoylepublished hislaw,theFrenchscientist JosephLouisGay-Lussacpublishedtwofurthergaslaws.One JacquesCharles.Charles'slawstatesthat:\n\nForaconstantmassofgasataconstantpressure,thevolumeoccupied bythegasisproportionaltoitsabsolutetemperature.\n\nThislaw canbeshown in symbols as:\n\nAbsolutetemperature/K\n\nfigCGraphofdatafromCharlesslawexperiment."}
