{"id": "yph2_v1_u9_c10_pdf151_0632", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 9, "unit_name": "Nuclear Decay", "chapter_no": 10, "chapter_title": "9A Radioactivity", "section": "LEARNING OBJECTIVES", "content_type": "learning_objectives", "book_pages": [141, 141], "pdf_pages": [151, 151], "char_count": 315, "text": "LEARNING OBJECTIVES\n\n• Define theconcepts of nuclearbinding energy andbinding energy per nucleon.\n\n• Make calculations of nuclear mass,mass deficit and binding energy,including use of the atomic mass unit.\n\n• Describetheprocessesofnuclearfission andnuclearfusion,includingtheconditionsneededtomaintainnuclearfusion."}
{"id": "yph2_v1_u9_c10_pdf151_0633", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 9, "unit_name": "Nuclear Decay", "chapter_no": 10, "chapter_title": "9A Radioactivity", "section": "ENERGY-MASSEQUIVALENCE", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [141, 141], "pdf_pages": [151, 151], "char_count": 185, "text": "ENERGY-MASSEQUIVALENCE\n\nAnucleonhasamasswhichisapproximatelyequal to1unifiedatomicmassunit,u (=1.66x 10-27kg).The exact masses of a proton,a neutron and an electron are given in tableA."}
