{"id": "yph2_v1_u11_c12_pdf178_0732", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 11, "unit_name": "Astrophysics and Cosmology", "chapter_no": 12, "chapter_title": "11A Gravitational Fields", "section": "GRAVITATIONALFIELDS", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [168, 168], "pdf_pages": [178, 178], "char_count": 877, "text": "GRAVITATIONALFIELDS\n\nGravityisone of the mostobviousscientificphenomena andwehave studied itforavery long time.When ways.\n\nInNovember2014,theEuropeanSpaceAgencylanded aprobeonthecomet67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. Thismaynotsoundremarkable.WehavelandedprobesontheMoon,Mars,otherplanetsandmoonsof otherplanets.However,thesizeandmassof thiscometmeansthatthegravitational fieldissoweakthatit had toensure thatthelanderwas travelling at lessthan onemetrepersecond,and even then thelander bouncedsignificantly.\n\nHowever,gravityremains oneof theleastwell-understood areasofphysics.There are a numberof ona fundamental level.Asyet,nonehavebeenconclusive,butastheirsensitivityimproves,scientistshope thatwewillbe abletocollectenough experimental evidence toconfirm howgravityworks.Gravitywaves, quantumgravity andso-calledstronggravity arecurrent areas of interesttocutting-edgephysicists."}
