{"id": "yph2_v1_u11_c12_pdf183_0756", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International A2 Level Physics Student Book 2", "author": "Miles Hudson", "unit_no": 11, "unit_name": "Astrophysics and Cosmology", "chapter_no": 12, "chapter_title": "11A Gravitational Fields", "section": "ELECTRICANDGRAVITATIONALFIELDS", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [173, 173], "pdf_pages": [183, 183], "char_count": 593, "text": "ELECTRICANDGRAVITATIONALFIELDS\n\nYoumayhavenoticedsomethingfamiliarabouttheequations wehavebeenusingtocalculategravitationalforcesandfields. Mathematically,theyareofexactlythesameformasthosewe usedtocalculatetheforcebetweenchargedparticles,electric potentialandelectricfieldstrength.Theonlydifferencesarethe symbolsweusetorepresentthequantitiescausingthefields,and theconstantsofproportionality.Thesimilaritiescomefromthefact thatbothtypesoffieldareradialfromapoint.Theconstantsof proportionalitydependuponthewaytheforcesinteractwiththe Universe,andwith theunitsystemthatweuseinthecalculations."}
